msgid "Indicates that a node is included into a paradata node group. Standard members are the paradata-chain nodes (PropertyNode/DocumentNode/ExtractorNode/CombinerNode/ParadataNode); GeoPositionNode is additionally admitted so the per-graph georeferencing shift can be a member of the graph-scope ParadataNodeGroup (DP-65) — semantically valid only at graph scope. v1.6.8 (MIG1-A): source widened further with AuthorNode/LicenseNode/EmbargoNode so the graph-scope rights metadata (author/license/embargo) live as first-class member nodes of the graph-scope ParadataNodeGroup (DP-65), replacing the legacy graph.data['author\\_name'/'license'/'embargo'] fields — again meaningful at graph scope (anchored on the GraphNode via has\\_paradata\\_nodegroup)."
